IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc28-part24-s752`

-- ccc28-tests-part24-s752.l4 -- tests of section 752 (the definitions of PART XXIV). Expected values are written from the text:
-- the table entries are parsed from the lines of the source text by work/tables.py (not from the encoding), the rest are written by hand
-- from the words of the definitions. A listed provision is tested under the Code the text lists it in, and each paragraph's neighbours
-- (the section just outside the list, the subsection or paragraph just outside it, the day on either side of a date) are tested too.

§ `Test fixtures (not law)`

GIVEN source IS A `s 752 source of the offence`
      section IS A NUMBER
      subsection IS A STRING
      implication IS A `s 752 how the offender is implicated`
      committed IS A DATE
      intent IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 752 offence`
`s 752 test the offence` MEANS
    `s 752 offence` OF source, (`Provision of the Code` OF section, subsection), implication, committed, intent

GIVEN mode IS A `Mode of proceeding`
      maximum IS AN Imprisonment
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 752 test the limb` MEANS
    Punishment OF mode, maximum, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`

`s 752 test the offence now` MEANS
    `s 752 test the offence` `s 752 an offence under this Act as it now reads` 266 "" `s 752 convicted of the offence itself` (Date 1 1 2020) FALSE

`s 752 test the life limb` MEANS `s 752 test the limb` `by indictment` `imprisonment for life`

`s 752 test violence` MEANS `s 752 conduct in the offence` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE
`s 752 test endangering` MEANS `s 752 conduct in the offence` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE
`s 752 test psychological damage` MEANS `s 752 conduct in the offence` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE
`s 752 test no violence` MEANS `s 752 conduct in the offence` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`s 752 test violence against no one` MEANS `s 752 conduct in the offence` OF FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE

§ `s 752 "court"`

#ASSERT `s 752 court` TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- the court that convicted the offender, whatever s 2 says
#ASSERT `s 752 court` TRUE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- the court that convicted the offender, even if it is not a superior court
#ASSERT `s 752 court` TRUE NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- the court that convicted the offender, even if s 2 is not covered
#ASSERT `s 752 court` FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- not the convicting court but a superior court of criminal jurisdiction
#ASSERT `s 752 court` FALSE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- neither: "court means" closes the definition
#ASSERT `s 752 court` FALSE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING   -- not the convicting court, and whether it is a superior court is not covered

§ `s 752 "long-term supervision"`

#ASSERT `s 752 long-term supervision` `s 752 subsection 753(4)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 752 long-term supervision` `s 752 subsection 753.01(5)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 752 long-term supervision` `s 752 subsection 753.01(6)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 752 long-term supervision` `s 752 subsection 753.1(3)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 752 long-term supervision` `s 752 subparagraph 759(3)(a)(i)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 752 long-term supervision` `s 752 an order under none of those provisions` EQUALS JUST FALSE

